From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:48:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: phones and tablets (hybrid / QR code) in
 the shell's passkey dialog
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan B155. Since the app declares NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription (B154),
device/fido creates the hybrid (caBLE v2) discovery and //chrome offers the
phone path. The bridge had no view for its steps, so they fell into
DescribeStep's default case and the shell showed "This method isn't
available" (seen on Google sign-in with a passkey account).

- OACWebAuthn.h: steps PhoneQRCode, PhoneConnecting, PhoneConnected,
  TurnOnBluetooth, BluetoothOff, BluetoothPermission; mechanism kind Phone;
  error kind PhoneConnectionFailed; properties phoneQRCode (Chrome's
  cable_qr_string, only in the QR step), phoneStepAcceptsSecurityKey and
  bluetoothIsPowered.
- oac_webauthn.mm: maps kCableV2QRCode / Connecting / Connected / Error and
  kBlePowerOnAutomatic / kBlePowerOnManual / kBlePermissionMac; lists
  Mechanism::Hybrid; accept turns Bluetooth on (busy until the adapter
  reports power), continues once it is on, or opens System Settings ▸
  Privacy & Security ▸ Bluetooth, as Chrome's sheets do. "Use another
  method" is hidden while connecting, connected and after the phone error,
  as in Chrome. Updates on Bluetooth power changes.
- oac_webauthn_test_bluetooth.mm (tests only): --openarc-fake-bluetooth[=off]
  installs an always-allowed adapter that never finds a phone (off until
  turned on with =off), so the engine test reaches the QR step without real
  Bluetooth.
- device/fido: FidoDiscoveryFactory honours ScopedAlwaysAllowBLECalls (new
  IsActive()) like FidoRequestHandlerBase already does, so that stand-in
  works under a test runner whose responsible process lacks the Bluetooth
  usage description. No change for the app (it is its own responsible
  process and has the description).
